WEBVTT

01:42.039 --> 01:49.009
[Genius Girlfriend]

01:49.560 --> 01:51.950
[Episode 2]

01:53.120 --> 01:55.310
Now I'll call roll in student ID order.

01:55.310 --> 01:56.979
Let's all get to know each other,

01:56.979 --> 01:57.370
okay?

01:57.729 --> 01:58.979
-Okay.
-Okay!

01:59.370 --> 02:00.090
Lin Zhixia.

02:00.690 --> 02:02.650
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

02:00.900 --> 02:01.350
Here.

02:02.980 --> 02:04.140
So you're Lin Zhixia.

02:04.140 --> 02:04.470
Okay.

02:05.260 --> 02:06.070
Jiang Yubai.

02:07.530 --> 02:08.940
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

02:09.530 --> 02:10.259
Jiang Yubai?

02:11.180 --> 02:11.710
Not here?

02:13.910 --> 02:14.770
Chen Zhenghao.

02:14.900 --> 02:15.360
Here.

02:16.210 --> 02:16.940
Wang Qingyu.

02:17.130 --> 02:17.579
Here.

02:18.690 --> 02:19.290
Excuse me.

02:21.130 --> 02:22.590
Late on the very first day?

02:22.620 --> 02:23.620
What's your name?

02:24.079 --> 02:24.810
Jiang Yubai.

02:36.340 --> 02:38.960
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

02:37.800 --> 02:39.600
Take the seat next to Lin Zhixia.

02:56.370 --> 02:59.990
[Reading Corner]

03:10.800 --> 03:16.200
[Reading Corner]

03:51.970 --> 03:53.170
It's been a long time.

03:54.090 --> 03:55.620
Yeah, it's been a long time.

03:59.780 --> 04:01.020
Hello.

04:02.250 --> 04:07.210
My name is J-J-J-J-Jiang

04:07.780 --> 04:08.580
Yubai.

04:10.410 --> 04:14.020
J-J-J-J-Jiang Yubai?

04:16.630 --> 04:18.890
Then call me L-L-L-L-Lin Zhixia.

04:23.220 --> 04:25.770
You've... gotten so tall.

04:26.560 --> 04:29.190
Yeah, I-I grew up.

04:54.130 --> 04:54.730
Five yuan.

04:57.450 --> 04:57.930
Bro,

04:58.800 --> 05:00.730
those are some pretty niche shoes.

05:01.160 --> 05:02.420
You've got good taste.

05:03.190 --> 05:04.600
Nah, I just threw them on.

05:06.510 --> 05:07.920
I forgot to introduce myself.

05:07.920 --> 05:08.930
I'm Duan Qiyan.

05:09.270 --> 05:10.270
We're in the same class.

05:10.270 --> 05:11.040
Aren't you Jiang Yubai—

05:11.040 --> 05:13.170
the second-best student in our class?

05:14.980 --> 05:16.830
Well, if you don't count Lin Zhixia,

05:16.830 --> 05:18.400
you'd be first in our class.

05:20.480 --> 05:22.430
How can we just leave Lin Zhixia out?

05:22.430 --> 05:23.690
She's the top student.

05:24.000 --> 05:25.270
Still, it's different.

05:25.270 --> 05:27.600
Her mind works on a whole different level.

05:29.000 --> 05:30.000
Not necessarily.

05:30.360 --> 05:32.690
There's always someone better out there.

05:34.720 --> 05:36.520
You're the first person I've met

05:36.600 --> 05:38.530
who dares to challenge Lin Zhixia.

05:38.920 --> 05:40.050
Just giving it a try.

05:41.680 --> 05:43.310
I just noticed how tall you are.

05:43.310 --> 05:44.640
Do you play basketball?

05:45.040 --> 05:45.510
Yeah.

05:49.040 --> 05:49.630
Me too.

05:50.070 --> 05:51.800
Let's play a game after school.

05:51.930 --> 05:52.430
Sure.

05:53.040 --> 05:53.659
Awesome.

05:55.300 --> 05:57.360
Let's meet at the court after school.

06:19.930 --> 06:20.660
Jiang Yubai.

06:21.110 --> 06:24.240
I heard you transferred here
from a school in Singapore.

06:24.830 --> 06:25.270
Yeah.

06:25.680 --> 06:27.630
So, is school in Singapore

06:27.630 --> 06:29.190
very different from ours?

06:29.600 --> 06:31.600
Are there lots of foreigners there?

06:33.100 --> 06:35.500
Actually, most of them are ethnic Chinese.

06:37.000 --> 06:39.690
I heard littering is illegal in Singapore—

06:39.810 --> 06:40.540
is that true?

06:40.750 --> 06:41.500
Really?

06:43.000 --> 06:43.750
Maybe.

06:44.040 --> 06:46.370
I've never broken the law,
so I'm not sure.

06:50.360 --> 06:52.040
I read in a book

06:52.480 --> 06:55.270
that Singapore is known
as the Garden City.

06:55.830 --> 06:57.390
Behind those strict regulations

06:57.390 --> 06:59.120
lies a kind of social contract.

06:59.120 --> 07:01.040
Citizens give up a degree of freedom

07:01.040 --> 07:01.560
in exchange

07:01.560 --> 07:04.040
for an exceptionally clean
and orderly environment.

07:04.040 --> 07:05.070
It's a city-state

07:05.070 --> 07:07.600
built through extraordinary planning

07:07.830 --> 07:09.270
under conditions of

07:09.270 --> 07:11.070
extreme resource scarcity.

07:17.680 --> 07:20.480
Why do you sound like
a robot answering questions?

07:52.830 --> 07:53.560
Jiang Yubai!

07:56.630 --> 07:57.680
Isn't it wild that we keep

07:57.680 --> 07:58.830
running into each other?

07:58.830 --> 08:00.690
Well, what are you doing tonight?

08:02.720 --> 08:03.130
I...

08:03.130 --> 08:05.360
I was wondering
if you'd like to come over tonight.

08:05.360 --> 08:06.070
We can watch

08:06.070 --> 08:07.800
the Lakers vs. Celtics replay together.

08:07.800 --> 08:09.400
It's the game of the century.

08:21.250 --> 08:22.580
What are you looking at?

08:24.360 --> 08:25.360
Come on, let's go.

08:25.450 --> 08:26.770
I've got tons of snacks

08:27.040 --> 08:28.500
and a huge sneaker collection.

08:28.500 --> 08:30.230
We can check them out together.

08:31.500 --> 08:32.169
Sure.

08:32.429 --> 08:32.960
Let's go.

08:33.500 --> 08:34.770
What do you like to do in your free time?

08:34.770 --> 08:36.460
Do you like playing soccer,

08:36.770 --> 08:37.510
video games,

08:37.840 --> 08:38.730
or...

08:48.120 --> 08:49.530
Jiang Yubai...

08:51.820 --> 08:54.220
Why do I feel like
something's off with him?

09:01.390 --> 09:02.590
It's been a long time.

09:03.510 --> 09:05.040
Yeah, it's been a long time.

09:06.630 --> 09:08.670
Then what did you eat in Singapore?

09:10.080 --> 09:11.390
Just food.

09:15.320 --> 09:17.940
Why did I ask something like that?

09:19.560 --> 09:21.700
Would he think I'm weird?

10:32.240 --> 10:35.910
[Jiang Yubai]

10:34.770 --> 10:36.790
I got into
No. 1 High School's experimental class.

10:36.790 --> 10:38.790
We're going to be classmates again.

10:46.650 --> 10:47.460
Jiang Yubai,

10:48.100 --> 10:49.230
I couldn't sleep,

10:49.600 --> 10:51.400
so I got up to leave you a message.

10:52.410 --> 10:53.170
Honestly,

10:53.250 --> 10:54.340
I've imagined

10:54.340 --> 10:56.030
our reunion countless times.

10:56.630 --> 10:58.370
But today's

10:59.120 --> 11:01.500
was way more awkward than I expected.

11:02.170 --> 11:04.120
Maybe it was
because we couldn't keep in touch,

11:04.120 --> 11:06.050
or maybe we'd been apart for so long

11:06.150 --> 11:08.750
that seeing each other again
felt unfamiliar.

11:09.320 --> 11:11.580
Anyway, I want to be honest with you—

11:12.290 --> 11:14.600
things felt off between us today.

11:31.380 --> 11:33.370
Actually, I felt the same way.

11:33.020 --> 11:41.130
[Lin Zhixia]

11:34.750 --> 11:37.480
I even bought strawberry milk
after class today,

11:37.600 --> 11:39.660
but I've been too shy to give it to you.

11:41.250 --> 11:47.950
[Jiang Yubai]

11:45.240 --> 11:47.150
I can't let something
weigh on my mind overnight.

11:47.150 --> 11:48.550
It's so much easier
to just say it out loud.

11:48.010 --> 11:55.610
[Lin Zhixia]

11:49.440 --> 11:52.100
Otherwise, overthinking is
just inefficient.

11:52.700 --> 11:53.130
Haha.

11:53.890 --> 11:54.860
That's so you.

11:58.080 --> 11:59.220
Why do you think

11:59.220 --> 12:01.480
we have no trouble talking on QQ?

12:02.290 --> 12:03.090
That's weird.

12:06.340 --> 12:08.530
Maybe we're just used to it.

12:12.050 --> 12:14.650
Anyway, I'll do my best to
get over it tomorrow.

12:15.740 --> 12:16.410
Me too.

12:17.080 --> 12:18.140
Let's ease into it.

12:25.580 --> 12:27.580
There's one more thing I need to fix.

12:28.620 --> 12:31.150
Today, when you asked
what I ate to get so tall,

12:31.650 --> 12:33.580
I just blurted out, "Food."

12:34.360 --> 12:36.020
It was a pretty stupid answer.

12:36.100 --> 12:37.900
I've been regretting it all day.

12:39.910 --> 12:48.240
[Haha. Then answer me again.]

12:40.890 --> 12:42.270
Then answer me again.

12:54.750 --> 12:57.320
Actually, I was shorter than you
when we were kids.

12:57.320 --> 12:59.050
That was a real blow to my pride.

12:59.200 --> 13:00.000
So when I was abroad,

13:00.000 --> 13:01.770
I made sure to
sleep by 8 or 9 every night.

13:01.770 --> 13:03.770
I worked really hard to grow taller.

13:06.940 --> 13:07.940
A little too hard.

13:08.440 --> 13:09.900
You've overshot the mark.

13:26.460 --> 13:27.520
What are you doing?

13:29.290 --> 13:30.580
I saw you were asleep,

13:30.580 --> 13:32.410
so I didn't wake you up.

13:36.460 --> 13:38.260
Who were you just chatting with?

13:39.150 --> 13:41.610
I had something urgent
to confirm, Brother.

13:42.390 --> 13:44.480
What was so urgent that
it had you grinning like that?

13:44.480 --> 13:45.940
Let me see who you were chatting with.

13:45.940 --> 13:47.150
It's the middle of the night.

13:47.150 --> 13:48.350
Who was it? Let me see.

13:48.390 --> 13:49.630
What are you doing?

13:49.630 --> 13:50.840
I want to see who you were chatting with.

13:50.840 --> 13:52.790
-You can't invade my privacy.
-Let go.

13:52.790 --> 13:54.080
Let go. Let me see.

13:58.600 --> 14:00.320
The computer might break
if you just shut it down like that.

14:00.320 --> 14:01.390
-It's fragile. It's...
-You...

14:01.390 --> 14:02.600
-It might break...
-You're the one who insists on looking.

14:02.600 --> 14:05.330
-It could break like that.
-Keep your voice down.

14:06.100 --> 14:07.340
I'm going to bed.

14:07.600 --> 14:08.670
It's broken. It's broken.

14:08.670 --> 14:09.820
You can't just shut it down like that...

14:09.820 --> 14:10.720
Lin Zhixia!

14:41.870 --> 14:43.870
J-J-J-J-Jiang Yubai.

14:54.390 --> 14:58.000
L-L-L-L-Lin Zhixia.

15:00.620 --> 15:01.150
Morning.

15:02.120 --> 15:02.650
Morning.

15:07.370 --> 15:08.770
Ignoring air resistance

15:08.840 --> 15:09.770
and friction,

15:10.120 --> 15:11.170
suppose a car

15:11.320 --> 15:13.460
is traveling at 30 meters per second.

15:14.050 --> 15:15.960
The driver notices a hazard ahead

15:16.440 --> 15:18.840
and takes 0.5 seconds to react

15:19.010 --> 15:20.540
before hitting the brakes.

15:21.050 --> 15:23.320
If the hazard is 60 meters away

15:23.320 --> 15:25.030
from the car's initial position,

15:25.030 --> 15:27.670
will an accident occur?

15:29.360 --> 15:30.220
Tang Tingting.

15:31.150 --> 15:33.440
You answer. Will there be an accident?

15:39.050 --> 15:43.100
Will the car crash...

15:48.150 --> 15:48.650
Yes.

15:51.000 --> 15:52.460
It will definitely crash.

15:54.600 --> 15:56.060
Alright, you can sit down.

16:07.570 --> 16:08.480
You,

16:09.460 --> 16:10.460
what's your name?

16:12.510 --> 16:13.440
I'm Lin Zhixia.

16:14.740 --> 16:15.700
Lin Zhixia,

16:16.150 --> 16:17.670
don't think I can't see you.

16:17.670 --> 16:19.200
From the podium,

16:19.290 --> 16:21.220
I can see every little thing you do.

16:21.960 --> 16:23.200
Were you even listening?

16:23.200 --> 16:24.860
And yet you fed her the answer?

16:25.340 --> 16:26.750
Go on, explain it.

16:27.220 --> 16:28.880
Why will there be an accident?

16:31.150 --> 16:32.750
The car won't come to a stop

16:32.750 --> 16:34.030
until it's traveled 105 meters.

16:34.030 --> 16:35.630
Since 105 is greater than 60,

16:35.630 --> 16:37.160
an accident is inevitable.

16:37.480 --> 16:38.810
Ma'am, I was listening.

16:43.080 --> 16:45.140
Alright, fine, you calculated fast.

16:45.770 --> 16:46.960
But you've been reading something
unrelated to class this whole time.

16:46.960 --> 16:48.760
Did you think I wouldn't notice?

16:49.030 --> 16:50.960
What were you reading? Take it out.

17:01.750 --> 17:03.010
You were reading this?

17:04.240 --> 17:06.640
I've already studied 10th-grade physics,

17:06.920 --> 17:09.920
so I wanted to read about things
I haven't learned yet.

17:10.720 --> 17:11.180
Well...

17:12.500 --> 17:14.790
even so, you still can't read it
during class, right?

17:14.790 --> 17:16.920
This still counts as outside reading.

17:21.960 --> 17:23.619
That's all for today's class.

17:24.380 --> 17:25.380
Class dismissed.

17:31.310 --> 17:32.770
If you're going to do
outside reading in class,

17:32.770 --> 17:33.570
you should...

17:34.830 --> 17:36.160
at least do it like this.

17:36.350 --> 17:39.880
You should be considerate of
the teacher's feelings, you know.

17:41.720 --> 17:44.120
Does this really count as outside reading?

17:44.680 --> 17:45.280
Let me see.

17:56.690 --> 18:00.090
[Introduction to Modern Physics]

18:18.590 --> 18:20.570
Yesterday, your Chinese teacher told me

18:19.610 --> 18:25.360
[Class Meeting]

18:20.850 --> 18:24.480
that you guys have been
a bit disengaged in class lately.

18:28.280 --> 18:31.880
[Class Meeting]

18:30.480 --> 18:31.330
I understand.

18:32.150 --> 18:34.420
Students in the experimental classes
have always

18:34.420 --> 18:36.060
tended to focus more on
the science subjects.

18:36.060 --> 18:38.090
[Class Meeting]

18:36.480 --> 18:38.480
Your logical thinking skills
are quite strong.

18:38.480 --> 18:39.850
So you're very used to

18:40.030 --> 18:41.350
the instant feedback that comes

18:41.350 --> 18:43.080
the moment you solve a problem.

18:43.810 --> 18:44.720
But students,

18:45.200 --> 18:46.510
don't ever overlook

18:45.660 --> 18:48.550
[Class Meeting]

18:46.510 --> 18:48.680
the gradual development of expression

18:48.680 --> 18:51.540
and depth of thought
that studying Chinese brings.

18:53.110 --> 18:55.180
There's a tradition
in every class I teach.

18:55.180 --> 18:59.130
[Class Meeting]

18:55.220 --> 18:56.810
At the start of each school year,

18:56.810 --> 18:59.440
I organize a Reading Corner activity.

18:59.880 --> 19:00.830
You can each bring a book you'd recommend

19:00.830 --> 19:02.250
for the class reading corner,

19:02.250 --> 19:04.510
and then we can all borrow and share them.

19:04.640 --> 19:06.370
We can learn and grow together.

19:06.920 --> 19:08.520
So you can start thinking now

19:08.550 --> 19:10.550
about the books you'd like to bring.

19:29.610 --> 19:31.410
Do you still like drinking this?

19:42.220 --> 19:43.820
What are you doing? Let's go.

19:46.980 --> 19:49.910
For the reading corner,
which book are you bringing?

19:50.850 --> 19:52.110
I haven't decided yet.

19:53.140 --> 19:54.570
I'm sure I'll recognize your pick

19:54.570 --> 19:55.630
the moment I see it.

19:56.250 --> 19:57.180
That confident?

19:57.880 --> 20:00.140
Then I'm sure I'll recognize yours, too.

20:01.720 --> 20:04.380
You're still as competitive
as you were as a kid.

20:10.680 --> 20:11.140
What?

20:12.220 --> 20:15.290
How did you suddenly get so tall?

20:15.900 --> 20:17.720
When we were little,
you were only this high.

20:17.720 --> 20:18.640
Sorry,

20:18.720 --> 20:20.650
but that's never happening again.

20:23.270 --> 20:24.200
This is so great.

20:24.400 --> 20:26.900
We're much more comfortable
around each other than we were yesterday.

20:26.900 --> 20:27.350
Yeah.

20:28.090 --> 20:30.070
Thanks to you—you always just say

20:30.480 --> 20:31.610
what's on your mind.

20:32.030 --> 20:33.200
I held that in all day yesterday.

20:33.200 --> 20:34.660
That was really unlike me.

20:36.640 --> 20:37.400
You know,

20:37.400 --> 20:38.860
I don't have many friends.

20:38.960 --> 20:39.880
After you left,

20:40.270 --> 20:42.200
I tried making new ones.

20:43.590 --> 20:45.960
So I tried really hard to
start conversations

20:45.960 --> 20:48.440
and ask people to go to
the bathroom together.

20:48.440 --> 20:50.680
But after trying for a while, I realized

20:50.880 --> 20:53.440
people just have their limits.

20:53.880 --> 20:56.640
I'm just not very good at making friends.

20:57.740 --> 21:00.400
Like-minded people
naturally find each other,

21:00.420 --> 21:02.080
so there's no need to force it.

21:02.420 --> 21:04.680
See? Didn't we end up meeting again?

21:09.250 --> 21:10.590
I think you've changed.

21:11.240 --> 21:11.850
How so?

21:17.440 --> 21:18.480
I can't quite put it into words,

21:18.480 --> 21:19.480
but you just have.

21:23.250 --> 21:24.910
What about me? Have I changed?

21:28.110 --> 21:29.510
Your hair is a bit longer.

21:30.440 --> 21:31.500
Other than that...

21:32.200 --> 21:32.940
not much.

21:37.030 --> 21:38.510
Actually, I've been wanting to ask you.

21:38.510 --> 21:40.240
Why did you come back this time?

21:40.500 --> 21:41.360
Because of you.

21:41.820 --> 21:46.160
♪ The moment our eyes met,
my world came alive with color ♪

21:46.830 --> 21:51.200
♪ Could this be how love begins? ♪

21:51.290 --> 21:52.350
I mean...

21:51.720 --> 21:54.700
♪ These unspoken feelings
are so hard to figure out ♪

21:53.750 --> 21:56.310
just like iron carbide, whose hardness

21:55.280 --> 22:00.680
♪ Hidden deep within your gaze ♪

21:56.310 --> 21:58.030
is 5 times that of ordinary iron,

21:58.030 --> 21:59.160
but ordinary iron

21:59.160 --> 22:01.380
only turns into iron carbide
at high temperatures.

22:01.000 --> 22:05.430
♪ Sometimes, I imagine
drifting beyond the skies with you ♪

22:01.830 --> 22:03.240
If I were ordinary iron,

22:04.200 --> 22:05.980
you would be the high temperature.

22:05.980 --> 22:10.000
♪ Shimmering light
dances over the flower in bloom ♪

22:10.750 --> 22:12.240
I really came back because of you.

22:10.820 --> 22:13.890
♪ After all we've been through,
our fates remain intertwined ♪

22:13.330 --> 22:16.250
Because I feel like I'm a better person

22:14.570 --> 22:21.060
♪ Perhaps fate favors me now ♪

22:17.250 --> 22:18.720
when I'm with you.

22:24.740 --> 22:25.870
Where are you going?

22:26.900 --> 22:28.560
This way, I'm taller than you.

22:33.070 --> 22:35.470
Now that you're back,
will you leave again?

22:39.430 --> 22:43.770
♪ The moment our eyes met,
my world was filled with hope ♪

22:40.000 --> 22:42.260
Definitely not while I'm in high school.

22:42.880 --> 22:43.610
And

22:44.440 --> 22:48.800
♪ Dim tender touches turn out to be love ♪

22:45.660 --> 22:47.320
we can go to college together.

22:48.350 --> 22:48.810
Okay.

22:49.320 --> 22:52.150
♪ Unsettling thoughts at last unfold ♪

22:52.890 --> 22:58.170
♪ I return the moment you glance back ♪

22:58.610 --> 23:02.690
♪ If reunion is fated ♪

23:03.590 --> 23:07.510
♪ Wish upon that dust speck
amid flowing light ♪

23:08.430 --> 23:11.500
♪ After all we've been through,
our fates remain intertwined ♪

23:12.180 --> 23:14.790
♪ If only time could stand still ♪

23:16.230 --> 23:17.890
My computer really is broken.

23:18.960 --> 23:20.160
I'll tell Dad in a bit.

23:24.590 --> 23:27.120
My old back pain
is acting up again these days.

23:27.920 --> 23:30.000
Once you finish eating,

23:30.000 --> 23:32.310
take some food to your mom
at the supermarket.

23:32.310 --> 23:32.940
I'll go.

23:37.270 --> 23:37.830
Zhixia,

23:38.720 --> 23:40.850
how's the start of the new school year?

23:47.720 --> 23:49.520
Everything else is pretty good.

23:49.750 --> 23:51.200
But I don't know why.

23:51.880 --> 23:54.540
Zeqiu won't let me say
we're siblings at school.

23:55.350 --> 23:56.070
Lin Zhixia!

23:57.510 --> 23:58.090
You brat.

23:58.880 --> 24:00.610
Is that how you act as a brother?

24:00.750 --> 24:03.000
You won't even let her
call you her brother?

24:03.000 --> 24:04.460
She's playing the victim.

24:04.970 --> 24:05.750
Last night,

24:05.750 --> 24:07.270
she sneaked into my room
to use the internet

24:07.270 --> 24:08.530
and broke my computer.

24:09.090 --> 24:10.070
I didn't sneak in.

24:10.070 --> 24:11.870
I just didn't want to wake you up.

24:12.270 --> 24:14.720
Then who were you chatting
with in the middle of the night?

24:14.720 --> 24:15.400
Who?

24:17.460 --> 24:18.520
Who was it, Zhixia?

24:19.750 --> 24:20.550
Jiang Yubai.

24:21.550 --> 24:22.460
Jiang Yubai?

24:25.680 --> 24:27.940
Your deskmate from when you were little?

24:28.480 --> 24:30.010
He's my deskmate again now.

24:30.350 --> 24:31.030
So what?

24:31.550 --> 24:32.950
Everyone has a deskmate.

24:33.000 --> 24:34.440
Alright, stop arguing.

24:34.880 --> 24:37.610
Finish eating quickly
and bring food to your mom.

24:42.570 --> 24:43.970
Dad, she won't let me eat.

24:44.480 --> 24:45.090
I did not.

24:45.720 --> 24:46.550
You two...

24:56.590 --> 24:57.590
You're back, Mom.

24:58.270 --> 24:58.900
Yubai.

24:59.880 --> 25:01.400
You cooked for yourself?
What are you eating?

25:01.400 --> 25:03.330
Just whipped up something simple.

25:04.010 --> 25:06.210
Are you getting used to the new company?

25:06.310 --> 25:07.110
It's just the beginning.

25:07.110 --> 25:09.970
I'm unfamiliar with the work,
but it'll get better.

25:10.270 --> 25:11.400
What about your colleagues?

25:11.400 --> 25:12.220
What are they like?

25:12.220 --> 25:13.550
They are all quite nice.

25:14.160 --> 25:14.890
That's good.

25:18.960 --> 25:21.290
I was supposed to ask you these yesterday.

25:21.510 --> 25:22.720
But look at you.

25:22.880 --> 25:25.200
You ended up asking me everything first.

25:27.920 --> 25:28.750
How about you?

25:29.270 --> 25:30.810
Are you getting used to the new school?

25:30.810 --> 25:32.470
Very well. I'm very used to it.

25:32.770 --> 25:34.570
It's way better than Singapore.

25:36.480 --> 25:39.550
It seems you are very satisfied
with high school life.

25:44.640 --> 25:46.400
Your dad even said before

25:46.960 --> 25:48.550
that the divorce was between the adults,

25:48.550 --> 25:51.280
so there was no need
to transfer you back to China.

25:51.790 --> 25:52.790
I told him

25:53.290 --> 25:55.240
that you definitely wanted to come back.

25:55.240 --> 25:57.370
Your good friends are all here, right?

26:01.740 --> 26:02.440
Besides,

26:03.070 --> 26:04.870
you didn't like it there anyway.

26:06.270 --> 26:09.010
Right, my good friends are all here, too.

26:15.920 --> 26:17.480
What does "always arguing back" mean?

26:17.480 --> 26:20.050
You say one thing,
and Tang Tingting fires back with nine.

26:20.050 --> 26:20.550
Your daughter is here.

26:20.550 --> 26:21.420
Mom, time to eat.

26:21.420 --> 26:22.220
Coming.

26:23.220 --> 26:24.140
You are so sweet.

26:24.140 --> 26:25.330
Bringing food to your mom?

26:25.330 --> 26:26.190
Hello, Auntie.

26:26.720 --> 26:27.320
Good girl.

26:27.720 --> 26:29.610
Right, I wanted to ask you, sweetie.

26:29.610 --> 26:30.470
Does your class

26:31.050 --> 26:33.510
assign seats based on grades?

26:34.940 --> 26:35.740
Well...

26:35.760 --> 26:37.770
Since you two are
at opposite ends of the rankings,

26:37.770 --> 26:39.370
shouldn't you be deskmates?

26:40.900 --> 26:42.560
We aren't assigned like that.

26:44.090 --> 26:45.400
That's a real pity.

26:46.770 --> 26:47.970
That's okay, though.

26:48.400 --> 26:50.420
Even though you've never
been in the same class,

26:50.420 --> 26:52.530
you grew up together.

26:52.700 --> 26:54.290
So you're best friends.

26:54.680 --> 26:56.280
You need to keep an eye on her.

26:56.610 --> 26:58.250
She doesn't take studying seriously.

26:58.250 --> 26:59.380
You have to help her.

27:00.010 --> 27:00.680
Got it.

27:01.530 --> 27:02.380
I'm leaving, Mom.

27:02.380 --> 27:03.440
-Okay.
-Good girl.

27:04.810 --> 27:05.980
And one more thing,

27:07.070 --> 27:08.600
what is your favorite food?

27:13.010 --> 27:13.830
♪ Say hi ♪

27:14.140 --> 27:15.860
♪ We have different colors ♪

27:16.370 --> 27:18.110
♪ To me, say hi ♪

27:18.760 --> 27:20.540
♪ We share the same dream ♪

27:20.870 --> 27:22.640
♪ How lucky I am to have you ♪

27:32.460 --> 27:33.140
Tingting.

27:37.590 --> 27:38.380
Sweetie.

27:39.460 --> 27:39.900
Mom.

27:40.980 --> 27:42.700
Look what I bought you.

27:42.790 --> 27:43.520
Take a break.

27:44.110 --> 27:44.740
You bought these?

27:44.740 --> 27:45.740
Have some snacks.

27:47.090 --> 27:48.460
Strawberry milk,

27:48.610 --> 27:50.740
strawberry cookies and strawberry candy—

27:50.740 --> 27:52.460
Which supermarket had a big sale?

27:52.460 --> 27:53.940
I-I don't like sweets.

27:53.940 --> 27:55.340
Sweets make me break out.

27:55.850 --> 27:57.770
I asked Lin Zhixia about this.

27:58.500 --> 28:00.230
Lin Zhixia told you to buy this?

28:01.530 --> 28:02.400
No.

28:02.740 --> 28:03.500
Here's the thing.

28:03.500 --> 28:05.440
I-I asked her very carefully.

28:05.830 --> 28:06.420
She told me

28:06.420 --> 28:08.750
she eats these almost every day.

28:09.530 --> 28:10.570
I was thinking,

28:11.050 --> 28:13.110
she's so smart,

28:13.330 --> 28:15.860
and it must have something
to do with her diet.

28:16.720 --> 28:18.310
Are you saying her smart brain

28:18.310 --> 28:20.250
comes from eating these?

28:21.530 --> 28:23.550
Well, what if it works?

28:24.140 --> 28:25.010
Let's give it a try.

28:25.010 --> 28:26.290
Just eat this one, okay?

28:26.290 --> 28:28.290
Mom, you're being ridiculous.

28:28.290 --> 28:30.620
Your ignorance could make the local news.

28:31.940 --> 28:33.440
Are you going to eat it or not?

28:33.440 --> 28:34.810
I don't like sweets.

28:34.810 --> 28:35.810
I'm not eating it.

28:40.240 --> 28:41.310
Your MP3,

28:41.810 --> 28:43.500
your phone,

28:43.500 --> 28:45.160
and all other electronics...

28:45.180 --> 28:47.180
I'll eat it. I'll eat it. I'll eat it.

28:47.330 --> 28:48.160
Well...

28:48.530 --> 28:49.940
That's more like it.

28:49.940 --> 28:51.610
It's food, not poison.

28:52.570 --> 28:55.430
Take a big bite.
Why are you eating it like medicine?

28:56.460 --> 28:57.720
Hurry, drink this.

28:57.770 --> 28:59.300
Wash it down with it. Hurry.

29:01.310 --> 29:02.480
Tastes good, right?

29:06.700 --> 29:07.300
Good girl.

29:08.380 --> 29:10.240
I'll buy you more when you finish.

29:11.090 --> 29:12.290
Eat it all. Eat it all.

29:18.790 --> 29:20.640
It tastes so bad.

29:21.160 --> 29:23.510
I'll definitely break out tomorrow.

29:50.380 --> 29:51.330
About my book...

29:52.090 --> 29:53.090
Do you need a hint?

29:57.360 --> 29:58.680
[Natural Philosophy]

29:57.850 --> 29:58.380
This one.

30:02.700 --> 30:05.030
It's on the reading list
I gave you before.

30:14.000 --> 30:15.680
[Jiang Yubai]

30:17.880 --> 30:19.810
Have you decided what to read then?

30:24.050 --> 30:25.110
I've read them all.

30:27.180 --> 30:29.310
How many books have you actually read?

30:29.770 --> 30:31.500
I've read all the science ones.

30:35.530 --> 30:36.590
How about this one?

30:37.200 --> 30:39.460
I've only heard of it but haven't read it.

30:40.420 --> 30:42.420
Jin Baihui has put that one in.

30:42.740 --> 30:43.800
Right, Jin Baihui?

30:47.810 --> 30:50.500
Jin Baihui, you read novels, too?

30:51.140 --> 30:51.980
I thought

30:51.980 --> 30:54.460
you'd put a study guide in here.

30:55.980 --> 30:57.940
It's the only non-academic book at home.

30:57.940 --> 30:59.670
I don't know when it was bought.

31:17.050 --> 31:18.530
[I blew the exam today. I got one
fill-in-the-blank math question wrong]

31:18.560 --> 31:20.170
[and only scored 118. But my parents
said not getting a perfect score]

31:19.980 --> 31:21.090
blew the exam today.

31:20.190 --> 31:22.010
[is the same as failing completely.
They even said I'm good for nothing.]

31:21.810 --> 31:23.420
I got one
fill-in-the-blank math question wrong

31:22.030 --> 31:25.090
[I've really tried my best.]

31:23.810 --> 31:25.180
and only scored 118.

31:38.640 --> 31:38.850
[I'm so tired. I want to run away.
But where should I go?]

31:53.200 --> 31:54.500
Whose book is this?

31:57.290 --> 31:58.150
Isn't it yours?

31:59.290 --> 31:59.740
No.

32:01.140 --> 32:02.270
That's impossible.

32:03.140 --> 32:05.330
You should be the only one
in the class who thinks

32:05.330 --> 32:06.590
a freshman in high school

32:06.590 --> 32:08.250
should read this kind of book.

32:26.700 --> 32:28.500
-This train of thought...
-Sir.

32:29.530 --> 32:30.180
Hold on,

32:30.180 --> 32:31.010
let me check.

32:31.460 --> 32:32.290
Let me check.

32:33.700 --> 32:35.290
You should consider

32:35.290 --> 32:38.250
taking university-level
math qualification exams.

32:38.250 --> 32:40.850
If you pass,
you can go straight to university.

32:42.180 --> 32:43.420
Actually, I haven't decided yet

32:43.420 --> 32:46.020
whether I need
to enter university this early.

32:48.330 --> 32:48.930
All right.

32:49.420 --> 32:51.680
Go back and discuss it with your parents.

32:52.420 --> 32:53.020
Off you go.

32:53.460 --> 32:55.640
All right, that's all from me.

33:05.480 --> 33:06.050
Ms. Kong,

33:06.830 --> 33:09.090
can I take the math qualification exams?

33:09.680 --> 33:11.330
You just started
your first year of high school.

33:11.330 --> 33:12.660
Let's take it one step at a time.

33:12.660 --> 33:15.660
Isn't Lin Zhixia also
in her first year of high school?

33:16.180 --> 33:16.840
Here, look.

33:18.070 --> 33:20.140
Although you also
got a perfect score in math,

33:20.140 --> 33:22.530
Lin Zhixia solved the hardest
bonus problem

33:22.530 --> 33:25.130
and even came up
with two different solutions.

33:27.070 --> 33:27.700
In a while,

33:27.700 --> 33:29.900
there will be a provincial
youth math contest.

33:29.900 --> 33:30.920
If you get a good ranking

33:30.920 --> 33:32.110
in it,

33:32.220 --> 33:34.080
we'll talk about what comes next.

33:35.760 --> 33:37.210
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest

33:37.300 --> 33:41.040
[Contest Information]

33:54.740 --> 33:55.250
Oh no.

34:03.220 --> 34:04.290
Sorry, I'm late.

34:06.850 --> 34:09.840
The little genius finally
remembered her cleaning duty.

34:09.840 --> 34:11.300
Ms. Kong just called for me,

34:11.300 --> 34:12.480
so I was held up for a bit.

34:12.480 --> 34:14.130
It's fine. We're almost done here.

34:14.130 --> 34:15.210
You guys go home.

34:15.210 --> 34:16.570
I'll take care of the rest.

34:16.570 --> 34:19.610
You immortals should stick
to solving the mysteries of the universe.

34:19.610 --> 34:21.650
Leave small things like cleaning

34:21.650 --> 34:23.650
to us mortals.

34:29.010 --> 34:29.870
Tang Tingting,

34:30.210 --> 34:31.210
every time you call me an immortal,

34:31.210 --> 34:32.690
it really makes me uncomfortable.

34:32.690 --> 34:34.489
Could you just call me by my name?

34:34.860 --> 34:36.500
You're already out of touch
with reality anyway.

34:36.500 --> 34:38.230
Isn't that what an immortal is?

34:38.380 --> 34:39.460
Is there anything else in your head

34:39.460 --> 34:40.880
besides studying?

34:41.190 --> 34:43.389
Stop meddling in us mortals' business.

34:45.500 --> 34:46.530
If you have any problem with me,

34:46.530 --> 34:47.590
you can just say it.

34:48.730 --> 34:49.530
Look,

34:49.880 --> 34:51.570
I got these two big pimples on my face,

34:51.570 --> 34:52.730
all thanks to you.

34:53.190 --> 34:54.300
Can you stop telling my mom

34:54.300 --> 34:55.440
all that nonsense?

34:56.050 --> 34:56.650
This is...

34:57.400 --> 34:57.940
Zhixia,

34:59.340 --> 35:00.870
what is your favorite food?

35:03.170 --> 35:05.090
If strawberry cake
could improve intelligence,

35:05.090 --> 35:06.550
why not apply for a patent?

35:06.780 --> 35:08.090
Please tell my mom directly

35:08.090 --> 35:09.650
that your intelligence is genetic,

35:09.650 --> 35:10.940
and it can't be intervened.

35:10.940 --> 35:13.740
Tell her to stop making me
eat strawberry candies!

35:13.900 --> 35:14.830
That's not true.

35:14.860 --> 35:15.730
IQ heritability

35:15.730 --> 35:17.650
is around 40 to 60 percent.

35:17.860 --> 35:19.610
Genes have a strong influence,

35:19.610 --> 35:21.010
but it's not 100 percent.

35:23.130 --> 35:24.090
Oh my god.

35:24.090 --> 35:25.820
Now you're talking about this?

35:27.130 --> 35:29.060
Your mom asked me what I like to eat,

35:29.190 --> 35:32.010
but I didn't know she would buy it
and force you to eat it.

35:32.010 --> 35:33.210
The pimples on your face

35:33.210 --> 35:35.340
aren't necessarily from strawberry cake.

35:35.340 --> 35:37.380
It could be clogged pores caused

35:37.460 --> 35:40.460
by excess oil during puberty
and improper cleansing.

35:44.090 --> 35:45.650
Are you saying I don't wash my face?

35:45.650 --> 35:45.940
I...

35:45.980 --> 35:46.820
Wait.

35:47.500 --> 35:48.090
Tang,

35:48.610 --> 35:50.030
it's about time.

35:50.210 --> 35:50.860
We should go home.

35:50.860 --> 35:52.340
You don't need to smooth things over.

35:52.340 --> 35:54.940
Doesn't your dad
often compare you to her, too?

35:55.780 --> 35:57.400
It's fine. It doesn't bother me.

35:57.400 --> 35:59.460
Oh, so I'm the only one with a problem?

35:59.940 --> 36:01.010
Don't be like her.

36:01.010 --> 36:02.010
Stop pretending.

36:02.670 --> 36:04.230
Why are you yelling at me?

36:06.170 --> 36:06.980
Let's go.

36:07.460 --> 36:08.530
She already said

36:08.530 --> 36:09.790
she'd handle the rest.

36:09.860 --> 36:11.130
Might as well let her.

36:12.170 --> 36:12.700
Let's go.

36:16.500 --> 36:17.700
Thank you, immortal.

36:17.800 --> 36:19.060
Thank you, Lin Zhixia.

36:23.820 --> 36:24.460
Let's go.

36:32.670 --> 36:36.810
[Class Challenge Leaderboard]

36:33.690 --> 36:36.440
I can solve problems that others can't,

36:36.950 --> 36:40.540
[Gödel, Escher, Bach]

36:37.820 --> 36:39.020
but I can't figure out

36:40.150 --> 36:41.570
why I'm always

36:42.090 --> 36:43.350
an isolated solution,

36:44.790 --> 36:47.120
never part of anyone else's solution set.

37:04.300 --> 37:08.280
♪ With every breath, the shadows creep ♪

37:11.370 --> 37:14.570
♪ The devil in disguise ♪

37:15.970 --> 37:19.030
♪ Talking the sweetest lies ♪

37:22.940 --> 37:26.510
♪ It tries to drown me in my sleep ♪

37:29.160 --> 37:32.610
♪ And comes like a tide ♪

37:33.830 --> 37:38.430
♪ It hurts, but I'm too tired to hide ♪

37:39.080 --> 37:43.940
♪ Please hold me, help me
walk out of this endless night ♪

37:42.340 --> 37:43.260
Growing taller

37:44.350 --> 37:45.630
♪ Lost the light and power ♪

37:44.380 --> 37:45.710
is of some use after all.

37:45.880 --> 37:48.480
♪ Lost my will to fight ♪

37:47.530 --> 37:49.860
I find you always show up right on time.

37:48.890 --> 37:52.090
♪ Can you stay by my side ♪

37:50.500 --> 37:52.030
It's as if it was meant to be.

37:53.290 --> 37:56.170
♪ Be my light knight ♪

37:53.300 --> 37:53.860
What?

37:55.170 --> 37:57.490
I'm going to update
my Human Observation Diary.

37:57.490 --> 38:06.910
♪ Let's run away ♪

38:07.280 --> 38:09.890
♪ Towards the light ♪

38:11.030 --> 38:13.870
♪ With you, I'll win this fight ♪

38:15.210 --> 38:17.210
Let's make up for all the years
it stopped being updated.

38:15.790 --> 38:25.040
♪ Let's run away ♪

38:18.300 --> 38:18.920
How?

38:20.780 --> 38:23.110
Tell me what happened there.

38:23.380 --> 38:24.240
I'll record it.

38:25.910 --> 38:28.310
♪ No turn to black ♪

38:29.150 --> 38:33.120
♪ Your love will carry us
through the night ♪

38:34.390 --> 38:43.510
♪ Let's run away ♪

38:44.610 --> 38:45.960
♪ Towards the light ♪

38:46.010 --> 38:47.790
It turns out some understanding

38:47.790 --> 38:51.290
♪ With you, I'll win this fight ♪

38:48.690 --> 38:50.220
doesn't need to be rebuilt,

38:50.840 --> 38:52.230
even after years apart.

38:52.850 --> 39:01.970
♪ Let's run away ♪

38:53.820 --> 38:55.620
Just like after a system reboot,

38:56.900 --> 38:58.090
you are still my

38:59.440 --> 39:00.570
default setting.

39:02.920 --> 39:05.220
♪ No turn to black ♪

39:06.110 --> 39:10.040
♪ Your love will carry us
through the night ♪

39:11.710 --> 39:15.640
♪ You and I ♪

39:16.310 --> 39:19.680
♪ Long last night ♪

39:21.060 --> 39:23.100
♪ You and I ♪
